## Defense Mechanisms to Anticipate

### Defense 1: Speed Advantage
```
LotusBook's feed → Updates odds in 0.5 seconds
PHOENIX scraper → Receives update in 2-3 seconds

Result: We're always seeing slightly stale odds.
Counter: Don't compete on speed. Exploit OVERREACTIONS, not stale data.
```

### Defense 2: Bet Rejection
```
Agent places bet → "Bet under review" → Rejected
Grounds: Odds changed, stake too large, account flagged

Counter: Accept rejection gracefully. Never retry immediately.
The RL agent should learn from rejection patterns.
```

### Defense 3: Account Restrictions (Gubbing)
```
Week 1: Full access, normal limits
Week 2: Win 60%, limits reduced 40%
Week 3: Win 58%, limits reduced 80%
Week 4: Win 55%, limits reduced 98%
Week 5: Account closed

PHOENIX must stay UNDER the detection threshold.
```

### Defense 4: Market Suspension
```
Critical moment → Market suspended 30+ seconds
By reopening, odds have moved, edge gone

Counter: If suspended > 10 seconds, skip the opportunity.
Don't chase. The RL agent should learn this patience.
```

